Round 41 independent scoped intake (fresh 2026-10-09T20:52Z): **KEEP DRAFT while exact-head CI completes**.

Verified head: `065f5ab5da1bc5de74cbd3e4c360b51e09200687`, based on current main. The four product intentions are materially useful and remain reviewable:

- exact Claude hook ownership with sibling/user-hook preservation;
- generic JSON uninstall type validation and byte preservation on no-op;
- create-if-absent first publication of archive `latest`;
- sparse materialization of unchanged scan actions while retaining scan membership for reconciliation.

Current matrix snapshot is 14 success / 3 in progress / 8 queued / 0 failure. No merge or Ready transition is appropriate before the exact-head suite reaches a real terminal state.

Acceptance boundary:
- this does not add a MutationJournal, cursor/fence, watermark, or filesystem-freshness certificate;
- it does not skip the existing scan/hash/resolver/resource/admission work;
- it is scoped engineering toward P8-018/P8-019, but P8-018 still depends on incomplete P8-017 and P8-019 still depends on incomplete P8-018;
- the pointer-race repair alone is not full reproducible archive/report acceptance;
- original-TODO completion credit is therefore 0.

This PR and #195 overlap only in the v15 registry/verifier binding files. If both product sets are later composed, the actual union tree needs a fresh independent P/R/G review and binding; neither existing registry may be selected as proof for the union.

